  "name": "DEFCON Furs",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "DEFCON Furs is an annual gathering celebrating the furry fandom within the hacker and infosec community, held inside the larger DEF CON conference in Las Vegas, Nevada, each summer. It began as a room meetup for furries attending DEF CON and grew beyond what a hotel room could hold, with the first official event on July 27 to 30, 2017. It is produced by Hack Your Lives, a 501(c)(3) non-profit headquartered in Berkeley, California, whose mission is to let people \"hack their lives\" in a safe and supportive environment. Programming includes panels and talks on technical and community topics, workshops, social meetups and themed parties, and its badges serve as memorabilia and access tokens. It keeps close ties with Queercon.",
